# Fixture: same_ontology_different_serialization_a.ttl
#
# Purpose: paired with same_ontology_different_serialization_b.ttl. Both files
# encode the IDENTICAL ontology (Animal/Cat/Dog with a Cat→hasOwner-someValuesFrom-Person
# restriction). This file is the VERBOSE form: explicit blank node labels, triple
# order shuffled relative to the natural one, restriction written out as separate
# triples instead of inline.
#
# Canonicalizing both files must yield byte-identical output — the most important
# test of this component.

@prefix : <http://example.org/same#> .
@prefix owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .

<http://example.org/same> a owl:Ontology .

:Animal a owl:Class .
:Person a owl:Class .

:Dog a owl:Class .
:Dog rdfs:subClassOf :Animal .

:hasOwner a owl:ObjectProperty .

:Cat a owl:Class .
:Cat rdfs:subClassOf :Animal .
:Cat rdfs:subClassOf _:restriction_alpha .

_:restriction_alpha a owl:Restriction .
_:restriction_alpha owl:onProperty :hasOwner .
_:restriction_alpha owl:someValuesFrom :Person .
